WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:04.003
-As a candidate,
Donald Trump repeatedly promised

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:06.439
that rural America,
which he dubbed Trump country,

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:07.907
would improve
under his presidency.

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.242
But is that really the case?

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:11.344
This is "The Check In."

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:13.179
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.747
[ Bell dings ]

00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:17.617
Throughout his presidency,
Trump has consistently claimed

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:19.419
that now he's in charge,
everyone,

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:22.155
especially his supporters,
are coming out on top.

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:24.790
-America now is winning again.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.126
Some people are getting
a little tired of winning.

00:00:27.126 --> 00:00:29.561
The people of Missouri
are gonna go to your governor,

00:00:29.561 --> 00:00:30.729
and they're gonna say,

00:00:30.729 --> 00:00:33.266
"Governor, please,
go see the President.

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:35.935
We can't stand winning so much."

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:38.438
We are going to keep on winning.

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:39.672
We're going to win so much,

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:41.707
you're gonna get
so tired of winning.

00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:44.944
Just so tired.

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:46.979
-I'll give him credit
for one thing.

00:00:46.979 --> 00:00:49.482
He doesn't
overwhelm you with details.

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:50.716
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.716 --> 00:00:52.685
Also, I don't think he gets
how winning works.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.320
You don't get tired of it.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.322
I've never heard
a New England Patriots fan

00:00:56.322 --> 00:01:00.026
burning his Tom Brady jersey
and moving to Cleveland.

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:03.296
"Enough's enough, Brady!
I got January plans!"

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:04.530
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.498
Trump loves to say that,
thanks to this presidency,

00:01:06.498 --> 00:01:07.700
farmers, coal miners,

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.535
and residents of red states
are back.

00:01:09.535 --> 00:01:10.970
But in November,
"The Washington Post"

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.438
asked the question,
"Is Trump country

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:13.973
really better off under Trump?"

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:16.910
And their answer was no --
it's falling further behind.

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:19.545
And there's no better example
of that than West Virginia.

00:01:19.545 --> 00:01:21.648
You might remember that
when Trump visited West Virginia

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:24.517
in 2016, he made all kinds
of impossible promises

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:26.986
and even
pretended to be a coal miner.

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:28.121
-I'll put it on, right?

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:31.157
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:39.765 --> 00:01:42.535
-I've never seen someone
so proud of his ability

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:44.237
to put on and take off a hat.

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:45.505
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:48.808
He took off that hat like a dove
was gonna fly out of it.

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:51.477
"Ta-da!"

00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:53.345
Also, whoever picked
his hard-hat size

00:01:53.345 --> 00:01:56.115
did not take into account
Trump's giant ego.

00:01:56.115 --> 00:01:57.249
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.249 --> 00:01:59.252
I know next to nothing
about coal mining,

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.621
but I'm pretty sure
that's not how you do it.

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:04.857
Unless I'm wrong,
coal is generally not located

00:02:04.857 --> 00:02:08.761
under 4 to 6 inches
of loose dirt on the surface.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:10.262
I think he's mistaking
coal mining

00:02:10.262 --> 00:02:13.532
with clearing the driveway
after a light snowstorm.

00:02:13.532 --> 00:02:15.368
But Trump didn't just
act like a coal miner,

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:17.570
he also promised he'd put
coal miners back to work,

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.973
and as president,
he claimed he'd succeeded.

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:21.640
-It's really happening.
We are back.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.776
The coal industry is back.

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:28.014
We've ended the war
on beautiful, clean coal.

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:29.649
I will tell you,
you will look back,

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:31.951
and you will say
it was the single greatest vote

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:35.187
you ever cast,
and you are gonna be very proud.

00:02:35.187 --> 00:02:38.057
And for those miners, get ready,
because you're gonna be

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:40.527
working your asses off,
all right?

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:42.095
-So there you go.
Trump says he's ended

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:43.462
the war on coal
and that coal miners

00:02:43.462 --> 00:02:45.031
would be
working their asses off,

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.899
but based on the actual facts,

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:49.869
it sounds like
their asses are still firmly on.

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:52.472
-Coal mines are closing
faster than ever.

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:55.007
-A bleak outlook tonight
on the coal industry.

00:02:55.007 --> 00:02:58.077
A brand-new report from CNN
suggests more coal plants

00:02:58.077 --> 00:03:00.280
have closed
during the first two years

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.714
of the Trump administration

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:04.517
than the first four years
of the Obama administration.

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:06.785
It's not because of regulations
but competition

00:03:06.785 --> 00:03:09.322
with cleaner,
cheaper forms of energy.

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:12.559
Another 20 plants
are expected to close this year.

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:14.961
-In fairness,
it isn't Trump's fault

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:16.229
that the mines are closing.

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:17.897
It's just the march of time.

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:19.598
It's the same reason
it's hard to find work

00:03:19.598 --> 00:03:21.134
as an abacus operator.

00:03:21.134 --> 00:03:22.435
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:24.437
And instead of facing
the reality that coal plants

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:25.972
are closing faster
under his presidency

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:27.239
than they did under Obama's,

00:03:27.239 --> 00:03:29.241
Trump keeps
insulting coal miners

00:03:29.241 --> 00:03:30.843
by insisting
that they're incapable

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:33.346
of doing anything
other than dig for coal.

00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:37.283
-Remember, I was here
just before the election?

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:39.785
And I brought a couple of guys
into a room, and I said,

00:03:39.785 --> 00:03:44.523
"Fellas, supposing
we teach you a new skill.

00:03:44.523 --> 00:03:45.925
Supposing we teach you, like,

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:49.929
how to make little widgets
or gidgets or gadgets or...?"

00:03:49.929 --> 00:03:51.764
These are big, strong
coal miners.

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:54.734
They said,
"Sir, we want to dig coal."

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:58.103
I said, "I agree with you!
I agree."

00:03:58.103 --> 00:04:00.440
-Well, maybe they would've
answered differently

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.007
if you had said,
"We'd like to train you

00:04:02.007 --> 00:04:04.643
to transition to another field
of energy development

00:04:04.643 --> 00:04:05.778
that's cleaner and safer

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:07.313
with better
long-term prospects,"

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:10.516
instead of, "Do you fellas wanna
make widgets and gidgets?"

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:11.884
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:15.621
"Giguh-guh-uhhh!
Wigi-gigi-guh."

00:04:15.621 --> 00:04:17.423
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:20.993
Also, they told you they didn't
want to learn new skills?

00:04:20.993 --> 00:04:22.961
Are you sure it wasn't
just an assumption you made

00:04:22.961 --> 00:04:24.931
like you did in an interview
with "Playboy" magazine

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:27.033
back in 1990
when you proclaimed,

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:28.700
"If had been the son
of a coal miner,

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:30.136
I would've left the damn mines,

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:32.271
but most people
don't have the imagination

00:04:32.271 --> 00:04:34.974
or whatever to leave their mine.
They don't have it."

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:37.509
Which is?
"'It' is an ability to become

00:04:37.509 --> 00:04:39.712
an entrepreneur,
a great athlete, a great writer.

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:41.647
You're either
born with it or you're not."

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:43.415
And by "it,"
he, of course, means

00:04:43.415 --> 00:04:45.451
a wealthy father
who cheated on his taxes.

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:46.585
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.585 --> 00:04:47.987
And don't take it from me.

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:51.057
Even experts on coal mining
in states like Pennsylvania

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:53.192
and West Virginia
said that Trump's lies

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:55.361
are actually hurting
the coal miners

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:57.096
he claims to be saving.

00:04:57.096 --> 00:04:58.631
-He's lying to them.

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:01.200
-For 52 years,
Art Sullivan worked in

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.569
and consulted on mines
around the world.

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:06.205
And he bristles every time
he hears the President

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:08.941
claim to be the savior of coal.

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:10.343
-And that really disturbs me,

00:05:10.343 --> 00:05:12.845
because these
are really good people.

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:15.915
-Do you feel the President gave
these communities false hope?

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:18.651
-In my opinion?
Absolutely.

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:21.220
I mean, I'm an expert.
He's not.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:23.755
If you spend several years
working coal mines,

00:05:23.755 --> 00:05:26.858
you're going to come
to understand electricity,

00:05:26.858 --> 00:05:28.761
hydraulics, mechanics.

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:32.699
I see no limitation on
the average coal miner's ability

00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:35.501
to transition
into any other field.

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:37.470
-That's right.
Coal miners are qualified

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:39.471
in electricity, hydraulics,
and mechanics.

00:05:39.471 --> 00:05:42.542
Meanwhile, Trump isn't even
qualified to be the canary.

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:44.744
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.744 --> 00:05:47.713
So, Trump promised that cutting
regulations on power plants

00:05:47.713 --> 00:05:49.949
would help bring back jobs
in rural America.

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:51.984
He also promised
that cutting those regulations

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:55.154
would not impact the quality
of the air and water.

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:56.722
-We want a clean environment.

00:05:56.722 --> 00:05:59.058
We want a strong, beautiful,
clean environment.

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:03.195
I want clean air,
I want crystal-clean water.

00:06:03.195 --> 00:06:04.496
And we've got it.

00:06:04.496 --> 00:06:09.768
We've got the cleanest country
in the planet right now.

00:06:09.768 --> 00:06:12.104
There's nobody cleaner than us.

00:06:12.104 --> 00:06:14.239
And it's getting
better and better.

00:06:14.239 --> 00:06:16.709
-Can we start
by cleaning you off first?

00:06:16.709 --> 00:06:18.077
[ Laughter ]

00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:19.979
You can't claim
we're the cleanest country

00:06:19.979 --> 00:06:22.348
when the President looks like
he just lost a challenge

00:06:22.348 --> 00:06:24.684
to eat the world's
hottest jalapeño pepper.

00:06:24.684 --> 00:06:25.818
[ Laughter ]

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:27.352
"Don't worry --
my stomach can handle --

00:06:27.352 --> 00:06:30.289
Oh!
I'm shvitzing right away."

00:06:30.289 --> 00:06:32.091
So, there you go.
Coal mines might be

00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:34.360
closing faster under Trump,
but at least they still have

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:36.996
clean air to breathe
and clean water to drink, right?

00:06:36.996 --> 00:06:39.264
-The Environmental
Protection Agency

00:06:39.264 --> 00:06:42.368
is considering rolling back
regulations on mercury.

00:06:42.368 --> 00:06:44.670
It's a neurotoxin
that can lead to brain damage,

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:48.541
learning disabilities, and
other birth defects in children.

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:50.375
-The Environmental Protection
Agency announced

00:06:50.375 --> 00:06:52.845
the proposal today,
saying that the cost

00:06:52.845 --> 00:06:55.915
of these regulations
outweighs the health benefits.

00:06:55.915 --> 00:06:57.817
Remind us again why we care

00:06:57.817 --> 00:06:59.519
about mercury
getting into the air.

00:06:59.519 --> 00:07:01.320
-It's a powerful neurotoxin.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.823
There are also
other hazardous air pollutants

00:07:03.823 --> 00:07:05.891
that are emitted
along with mercury.

00:07:05.891 --> 00:07:08.160
-So you might have expected
Trump to neglect the blue states

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:09.528
that didn't vote for him.

00:07:09.528 --> 00:07:11.731
I wouldn't be surprised
if he started dumping mercury

00:07:11.731 --> 00:07:14.367
over New York
out of Air Force One.

00:07:14.367 --> 00:07:17.236
"Don't breathe in, losers!"

00:07:17.236 --> 00:07:18.671
But this is Trump country.

00:07:18.671 --> 00:07:20.306
These are people
he promised to help,

00:07:20.306 --> 00:07:22.608
and if this keeps up,
Trump might need a shovel

00:07:22.608 --> 00:07:24.243
to dig himself out of this hole.

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:25.678
This has been "The Check In."

00:07:25.678 --> 00:07:27.780
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:29.715
[ Bell dings ]

